    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0306" n="1040" xml:id="pg1040"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Gibbs.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-02-21"><hi rendition="#italic">February 21,
                        1879</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 136.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 300, in relation to the decision of the Peruvian Government to pay the
                    claims of the members of the Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon, and to say
                    in reply that I have caused the decision to be communicated to the persons
                    interested. I have no doubt the success of your representations in their favor
                    will be fully appreciated.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. M. Evarts.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
